<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grenadines</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grenadines are a chain of about 600 small islands and islets in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windward-islands">Windward Islands</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, between Saint Vincent and Grenada. The northern islands, including Bequia, Mustique, Canouan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-island">Union Island</a>, belong to Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, and the southern ones, such as Carriacou and Petite Martinique, to Grenada. They live by fishing, sailing and tourism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grenadines.jpg" alt="Grenadines" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alison DeGraff · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grenadines.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
